---
name: sqlalchemy-orm
description: PropIQ SQLAlchemy ORM conventions and standards.
---

# Authority

DATABASE_SCHEMA_DESIGN.md is authoritative.

This skill only defines implementation conventions.

# ORM Standards

- SQLAlchemy 2.x typed ORM.
- Use DeclarativeBase.
- Use Mapped[] and mapped_column().
- PostgreSQL is the target database.

Example:

class User(Base):
    __tablename__ = "users"

    id: Mapped[UUID]
    email: Mapped[str]

# Primary Keys

- UUID primary keys.
- Generated server-side where possible.
- Never use integer identity keys for domain entities.

# Timestamps

Every mutable entity includes:

created_at
updated_at

UTC only.

# Naming

Tables:
snake_case plural

Columns:
snake_case

Indexes:
ix_<table>_<column>

Foreign Keys:
fk_<source>_<target>

# Relationships

Always define both sides.

Use lazy="selectin".

Avoid circular imports.

# Enums

Use Python Enum.

Persist as PostgreSQL ENUM.

# Constraints

Represent constraints both:

- database level
- application validation level

# Forbidden

No business logic.

No calculation logic.

No service logic.

ORM models are persistence only.